Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Physical branding, intuitive dock and sharp waving startup with screen-only fullscreen.
Dependencies: Completed workstreams 19 and 22.

Purpose
-------
Make the hardware markings look manufactured rather than like colored stickers,
clarify toolbar actions, position notifications below the website wordmark and
provide a sharp animated startup plus a genuine live LCD-only fullscreen mode.

Tasks
-----
[x] Replace only the front bezel logo with monochrome printed text.
[x] Add an original raised geometric ZANARK maker badge in matching shell plastic.
[x] Place scene notifications directly below the website logo; retain modal notices.
[x] Distinguish put-down/cartridge/save/slots/restart and inspection-return icons.
[x] Add screen-only fullscreen preserving the current native framebuffer and keyboard input.
[x] Raise startup raster resolution and animate a gentle wordmark wave.
[x] Complete focused browser and visual review, including reduced motion and error recovery.
[ ] Pass normal release gates and verify actual production behavior.
[ ] Refresh affected guides/images/visual README and record final evidence.

Acceptance criteria
-------------------
Front bezel has grayscale text only, not a purple orbital sticker.
Top maker mark has real raised geometry and an original non-Nintendo treatment.
Notifications align below the header logo without blocking scene input.
Named icons have distinct shapes and retain usable 44px targets at phone sizes.
LCD-only fullscreen shows actual running frames, accepts existing controls and
returns without a new runtime, reset, checkpoint restore or changed power intent.
Startup uses a 960x640 raster with unchanged 3:2 logical composition, contained
orbit and gentle wordmark wave; reduced motion is static and timing is retained.

Completion evidence
-------------------
Syntax, build and 11 units pass. Five focused actual Edge cases pass in1.1m,
and the same five pass with explicit Chromium/SwiftShader in2.2m.
Final expanded quick-actions case passes Edge46.3s: simulated request refusal
recovers visibly, live fullscreen pixels match the native framebuffer before
and after actual input, both Escape and exit button preserve runtime identity.
Existing autosave/slots/restart checks remain. Reviewed actual startup,
monochrome print, raised maker mark, 320px notices/dock and fullscreen captures.
This is technical/visual review, not new user aesthetic acceptance.
Normal hosted release and production verification remain pending.
Observed blur sources: startup was drawn at native 240x160 and magnified with
linear texture sampling, with an additional 8px logo shadow on that small raster.
Native gameplay resolution/shader are not changed by the startup raster fix.

Completion log
--------------
2026-11-04: User supplied physical-console examples and requested monochrome
bezel lettering, an original embossed Zanark mark, header notifications,
